0..74 Comment "// Three routes by which a theory could smuggle axiom K past the identity,"
75..99 Comment "// each refused by name."
100..102 Comment "//"
103..178 Comment "// A theory\'s law is a hypothesis its models prove, so no law makes K true."
179..245 Comment "// A model may admit a law only when its host asserts the law of a"
246..323 Comment "// primitive. No host asserts K. So a model that admits the collapsing law at"
324..399 Comment "// a carrier whose loops differ is refused `UnprovenLaw.Admitted`. A rule\'s"
400..474 Comment "// left side is an operation application. A rule whose left side is a bare"
475..545 Comment "// variable is refused `UndescribedMember.LhsNotOperation`. So no rule"
546..624 Comment "// matches a path by its mere existence. The law form carries a path at a sort"
625..702 Comment "// or a host type, not a path of paths. So a law about the native identity is"
703..779 Comment "// refused `MalformedForm`. When the form grows, the first wall still holds:"
780..832 Comment "// each model proves the law, and no host admits it."
833..835 Comment "//"
836..911 Comment "// `CollapsedInteger` admits the law at `Integer`. `RuledK` writes the rule"
912..982 Comment "// from a variable. `WithK` states K for the native identity as a law."
983..985 Comment "//"
986..1060 Comment "// - see: `../../model/modules/law-collapsed.gandr` — the accepted model"
1062..1093 Comment "/// A sort whose loops are one."
